{
  "_readme": [
    "Slot table: our own description of what each pre-recorded motion does.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: slot internals cannot be read back from the robot.",
    "'phorce list' tells you a slot's id and name and nothing else. So we",
    "describe them here, and the decision layer picks a slot by matching this.",
    "",
    "POSES (radians, axes 0-3): derived from the CAD mechanism, not taught.",
    "The robot is a parallelogram rocker -- four arms swing together about Y",
    "and the platform rides level on bearings at the arm tops. So every pose",
    "commands the SAME angle on all four axes: +x sway is positive, -x is",
    "negative, and centre motions return to 0. Giving the axes different",
    "angles would fight the closed linkage (and visibly detaches the platform",
    "in the RViz model, which cuts the loop).",
    "",
    "Still 'placeholder: true' because nothing has been taught on the real",
    "robot -- once phorce Studio motions exist, replace these with read-back",
    "angles and drop the flag."
  ],
